{"mls":"R1710862","addr":"4492 Humphrey Road","muni":"Humphrey town","town":"Humphrey","county":"Cattaraugus","zip":"14741","ll":[42.205587,-78.541014],"status":"Active","type":"Single Family","units":1,"beds":3,"baths":2,"sqft":1690.0,"year":1900,"lot":0.499,"dom":45,"price":199900,"orig":249900,"chg":"Price Change","tax":2403,"tax_mls":true,"hoa":null,"office":"Howard Hanna Professionals - Olean","phone":"716-378-7039","hhp":true,"remarks":"Class is out — permanently. The former Humphrey Elementary School has been reborn as a one-of-a-kind residence in the heart of Cattaraugus County's Enchanted Mountains. Just 12 minutes to Holiday Valley Ski Resort, 14 minutes to Ellicottville's downtown, 1 hour to Buffalo, and 12 minutes to Olean, this home is surprisingly convenient to amenities while still being out of town.\r\n\r\nSoaring ceilings and oversized windows give this three-bedroom, 1.5-bath home a sense of volume no ordinary house can match. Light pours across rooms built on a scale you simply don't find in new construction. The Great Room anchors it all, warmed by a wood stove that keeps winter propane costs refreshingly low.\r\n\r\nThoroughly updated with modern amenities, it includes all appliances and has a metal roof. Out back, a generous deck looks out over rolling hills — morning coffee, evening sunsets, and not much else to interrupt the view.\r\n\r\nLive in it, host in it, or both. The scale, the layout, and the story behind it make a compelling short-term rental in a region that draws visitors year-round.\r\n\r\nSome homes have history. This one has generations of it.","facts":[["Total rooms","7"],["Full baths","1"],["Half baths","1"],["Style","Historic Antique, Other, See Remarks"],["Stories","2"],["Building area (sq ft)","1,690"],["Heating","Propane, Baseboard, Hot Water"],["Basement","Crawl Space"],["Foundation","Block, Stone"],["Construction","Wood Siding, Copper Plumbing"],["Roof","Metal"],["Garage","No"],["Garage spaces","0"],["Parking","No Garage